preConditionHook:
// Brooks's glossary gap: the FIRST bar of a session opens beyond the prior
// session's extreme -- above the prior session's high (long) or below its low
// (short). Three sources quote the same glossary line; the whole-day high/low
// won over 'the prior session's last bar', the weaker reading and no cheaper
// once the day accumulator exists.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: a session starts when the
// wall-clock close date changes -- day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)),
// the EL twin's date > date[1]. IsFirstBarOfSession is INLINED rather than
// referenced, as the corpus does with every named composite, and the gate is
// structural rather than an independent filter: off the session's first bar
// the rule has nothing to say.
//
// prevHigh / prevLow ARE HighD(1) / LowD(1), which the twin calls and the
// engine does not expose. MEASURED (the highd/lowd register row): the day is
// the wall-clock CALENDAR date, the SAME boundary as date <> date[1]; xxxD(0)
// is the running value INCLUSIVE of the current bar; the functions return a
// -1 SENTINEL while fewer than that many complete days exist. The mirror
// keeps the running day extremes, rolls them at the date change and keeps the
// -1 sentinel as the initial value, so the guard means the same thing in both
// twins.
//
// WARM-UP, the one place the twins can differ, exactly as in
// FailedBreakoutOfPriorSessionExtreme: TradeStation's HighD reads the chart's
// own data and answers on the first evaluated bar, while this mirror sees
// only bars from Max Bars Back on. sawStart makes that honest -- a day is
// published as 'the prior session' only once its own first bar has been
// observed, so the mirror is silent through the first partial day and the
// first fully observed day and the two agree exactly from the second date
// change on. The mirror errs toward no signal.
//
// Not TrueGapBar (a whole-range gap over the PREVIOUS BAR, at any point of
// the chart) and not LargeGapVsAverageRange (the same bar-to-bar gap with a
// size term): the reference here is a session extreme and the rule can fire
// at most once a day. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    if (sawStart) {
        prevHigh = curHigh;
        prevLow = curLow;
    }
    sawStart = true;
    curHigh = high[0];
    curLow = low[0];
    firstBar = true;
} else {
    if (el_gt(high[0], curHigh)) curHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], curLow)) curLow = low[0];
    firstBar = false;
}
gapUp = firstBar && !el_eq(prevHigh, -1.0) && el_gt(open[0], prevHigh);
gapDn = firstBar && !el_eq(prevLow, -1.0) && el_lt(open[0], prevLow);
